    {
      "id": 223815,
      "name": "hstein3",
      "username": "hstein3",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/hstein3/{size}/2159_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-10-29T13:42:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Looking at other threads, I'm seeing people discuss powers that let you destroy cards&nbsp;(such as Omnitron-U or F6 Tempest)&nbsp;that lets you go after cards under a Villain card because those cards are still considered to be in play.</p>\n<p>Yet in this instance, Writhe can't destroy the&nbsp;<em>Shadow Cloak</em>&nbsp;because it's not \"in play\" when it's under a card.</p>\n<p>This seems inconsistent, unless there's some detail about when you can target cards under another card that I'm missing.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:03.630Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 18683,
      "topic_slug": "void-cloak-and-la-capitan",
      "display_username": "hstein3",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Looking at other threads, I'm seeing people discuss powers that let you destroy cards&nbsp;(such as Omnitron-U or F6 Tempest)&nbsp;that lets you go after cards under a Villain card because those cards are still considered to be in play.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yet in this instance, Writhe can't destroy the&nbsp;<em>Shadow Cloak</em>&nbsp;because it's not \"in play\" when it's under a card.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This seems inconsistent, unless there's some detail about when you can target cards under another card that I'm missing.&nbsp;</p>",
      "actions_summary": [
